Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:02.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Plot a point in space.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:02.33,0:00:04.09,Default,,0,0,0,,We need three axes:
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.09,0:00:05.86,Default,,0,0,0,,x, y, and z.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.86,0:00:07.81,Default,,0,0,0,,A point in 3D is
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.81,0:00:09.77,Default,,0,0,0,,written as x, y, z.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.77,0:00:11.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Start at the origin, and
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.70,0:00:13.63,Default,,0,0,0,,move 3 units along x.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.63,0:00:15.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Then 2 units
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.11,0:00:16.58,Default,,0,0,0,,parallel to y.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.58,0:00:18.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Finally, 5 units
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.20,0:00:20.35,Default,,0,0,0,,up, parallel to z.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.35,0:00:21.87,Default,,0,0,0,,So the point
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.87,0:00:23.90,Default,,0,0,0,,is (3, 2, 5).
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.90,0:00:25.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Plotting in 3D
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.23,0:00:27.00,Default,,0,0,0,,is just three steps.